UNAME(1)                       P32W Unix                        UNAME(1)

NAME
       uname - print the name of the system

SYNOPSIS
       uname [-snrvma]

DESCRIPTION
       uname prints the name of the operating system:

              P32W Unix

OPTIONS
       -s     the system's name (the default)
       -n     the node (machine) name
       -r     the release
       -v     the version
       -m     the hardware
       -a     all five

       Several fields are printed in that order (not the order of
       the options), separated by blanks; options may be combined,
       as in -sm. uname -a prints, for example,

              P32W Unix p32w 0.7 M7 p32w

EXIT STATUS
       0; 2 for an unknown option or an argument
       ("usage: uname [-snrvma]").

SEE ALSO
       uptime(1), who(1)

BUGS
       The node name is fixed (p32w) and cannot be set; there is no
       hostname command. The system's name has a blank in it, so
       uname -a has six words, not five.
